From: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa2-lite: use a translated SMMU domain for AP DMA

The uC stream must remain in an identity domain because modem firmware owns
its addresses.  The AP stream is different: all BAM descriptor FIFOs and
packet buffers are allocated or mapped through the DMA API.

Forcing the main IPA device into the Qualcomm identity-client list selects
the SDM630/660 SMMU bypass path.  On lavender the first TX then raises BAM
HRESP while reading the second word of the descriptor FIFO, followed by IPA
BAD_SNOC_ACCESS and the modem ipa_hal.c:2163 assert.  Leave only the uC
child in the identity-client list and require a translated domain for IPA
2.6L.

Also handle failure of the 32-bit DMA mask instead of ignoring it.

Signed-off-by: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 2fa412648..208a5a541 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -398,7 +398,6 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,adreno" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,adreno-gmu" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-mdss" },
-	{ .compatible = "qcom,ipa-lite-v2.6" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ipa-smmu-uc-cb" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdp4" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdss" },
diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
index 6369a3b..a6d9308 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
@@ -2000,6 +2000,7 @@ static int ipa_smmu_uc_ready(struct device *dev)
 static int ipa_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct iommu_domain *domain;
 	const char *name = "rmnet_ipa0";
 	struct ipa *ipa;
 	int ep, ret;
@@ -2057,7 +2058,21 @@ static int ipa_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
 				     "failed to set active IPA clock rate\n");
 
-	dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "failed to set 32-bit DMA mask\n");
+
+	domain = iommu_get_domain_for_dev(dev);
+	if (!domain)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "AP SMMU domain is not ready\n");
+
+	if (ipa->version == 26 && domain->type == IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDENTITY)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL,
+				     "IPA 2.6L AP stream cannot use SMMU bypass\n");
+
+	dev_info(dev, "AP SMMU domain type %#x\n", domain->type);
 
 	ipa_reset_hw(ipa);
 
